{
  "api": "openai",
  "from_version": "v0",
  "to_version": "v1.0.0",
  "summary": "v1 is a total rewrite requiring explicit client instantiation via `client = OpenAI(api_key=os.environ['OPENAI_API_KEY'])` instead of global state, changing all response objects from dicts to pydantic models requiring attribute access (`completion.choices[0].text`) with `model.model_dump()`/`model_dump_json()` conversion, and adding auto-retry with backoff, proper types, and automatic iteration for all `list()` methods replacing `.auto_paging_iter()`. All resource methods moved under `client` (e.g. `openai.Completion.create()` -> `client.completions.create()`, `openai.Image.create()` -> `client.images.generate()`, `openai.File.download()` -> `client.files.retrieve_content()`, `openai.FineTune.stream_events()` -> `client.fine_tunes.list_events(stream=True)`), config/module names changed (`api_base` -> `base_url`, `proxy` -> `proxies`, `InvalidRequestError` -> `BadRequestError`, `api_resources` -> `resources`), and all `a*` methods were removed in favor of the async client. Removed globals/classes/helpers (`api_key_path`, `app_info`, `debug`, `log`, `OpenAIError`, `ErrorObject`, `Customer`, `api_version`, `verify_ssl_certs`, `api_type`, `enable_telemetry`, `ca_bundle_path`, `requestssession`/`aiosession`, `Deployment`, `Engine`, `Audio.transcribe_raw`/`translate_raw`, `File.find_matching_files`, `embeddings_utils`) with replacements to `httpx`, `azure-mgmt-cognitiveservices` for Deployments, and the cookbook for embeddings_utils, plus Weights and Biases CLI split to its own package. Global `openai.*` client access remains only for REPLs/notebooks and application code must instantiate `OpenAI()` to avoid race conditions and allow mocking and connection cleanup.",
